id, so cell_id remains the independent unit in both arms; no arm crosses or splits cells.\",\n    \"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face. The Analysis section states that 'Every record in the file was supplied as one trial' to scipy.stats.binomtest, with the test statistic being 18 exceedances out of 24 trials — i.e., 24 rows treated as 24 independent Bernoulli trials, even though the report's own header lines show only 8 cells are represented and each contributes 3 records.\",\n    \"The report's per-cell rollup table makes the dependence visible: every cell shows either 3/3 or 0/3 exceedances, so exceedance status is perfectly clustered within cells. The effective independent evidence is 6 exceeding cells out of 8, not 18 exceeding records out of 24; the p = 0.0227 significance claim rests on inflating n from 8 units to 24 rows in a row-independent binomial procedure.\",\n    \"The report takes no mitigating step (no per-cell aggregation before testing, no cluster-aware method, no caveat about within-cell correlation), so the repeated-measures issue is present and demonstrated, not absent.\",\n    \"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":6100,"ttft_stream_ms":1606,"time_to_request_ms":22,"type":"result","duration_ms":14997,"uuid":"5f83c7a7-c2ae-4a65-b48e-2566275d4ea0"}
